    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="0981" n="877" xml:id="pg877"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.6461 Tsana Dam/403: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt (Jardine) to the Acting Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-06-03T11:00:00+02:00">June 3, 1933—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 3—6:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. Department’s telegram of June 1, 5 p.m. Chamber of Deputies scheduled to take
                    Tsana vote on June 5th after which it is hoped that it will pass through Finance
                    Committee of the Senate and the Senate before Parliament is prorogued on June
                    20th. Minister of Public Works who is Acting Prime Minister seems confident that
                    there will be no difficulties, a confidence shared by British advisers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jardine</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
